{"name":"Brandy","hex":"#dcb68a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Brandy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from English derived from brandy, an alcoholic liquor. Mostly seen in American usage during the 1970s and 1980s."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Brandy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brandy","blocks":[{"text":"Brandy is a liquor produced by distilling wine. Brandy generally contains 35–60% alcohol by volume and is typically consumed as an after-dinner digestif. Some brandies are aged in wooden casks. Others are coloured with caramel colouring to imitate the effect of ageing, and some are produced using a combination of ageing and colouring. Varieties of wine brandy can be found across the winemaking world. Among the most renowned are Cognac and Armagnac from southwestern France."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Cognac_glass.jpg/330px-Cognac_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandy","wikidata":"Q146470"},{"title":"Brandy (Scott English song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Brandy\", later called \"Mandy\", is a song written by Scott English and Richard Kerr. It was originally recorded by English in 1971 and reached the top 20 of the UK Singles Chart."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Brandy_by_Scott_English_US_single_variant_A.png/330px-Brandy_by_Scott_English_US_single_variant_A.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandy_(Scott_English_song)","wikidata":"Q959011"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Bodega-TioPepe-Jerez-Dsc02980.jpg/500px-Bodega-TioPepe-Jerez-Dsc02980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Bodega-TioPepe-Jerez-Dsc02980.jp